;; The crops' independence, stage by stage (doc/CROPS-SCORE.md, "Independence"): reviewed facts, read by bin/crops-score
;; (test/crops/score.ae). Read with the Clojure reader.
;;
;; Per crop, :stages, the facts of main (the checkout this file is on), and :at, the facts that differ at a held ref (by its
;; short name, as --ref and --newest give it), merged over them stage by stage. A stage:
;;   :read :eval :aot :print  the stage's pipeline: Arbace's path from the input to its output, with the inputs it consumes
;;                            (OCaml's Lambda, GHC's STG, rustc's and clang's IR, the helpers' dumps, installed headers)
;;   :judge                   what the crop's checks compare with at check time, every cell's (the references, the oracles)
;; and its fact:
;;   :score     1: no host toolchain at check time and no record of one consumed; 0.5: none at check time, but the stage consumes
;;              or compares with a record a host toolchain made, re-recorded by hand (or the toolchain runs only in the oracle
;;              tier, :phase :oracle, by hand at a tag); 0: a host toolchain runs at check time in the stage (a live dump, a live
;;              reference run, an installed tree of a toolchain's package read in place), or the stage does not exist on the ref
;;   :tool      the command; :host the host toolchains it needs (GT9's host names); :why the reason in a phrase
;;   :evidence  file:line (REF:file:line on a held ref) or a command, what shows it
;;   :steps     the gate steps that run the stage (the tree's test/gate/steps.edn, else its GT9 fragment): bin/crops-score
;;              scores 0 a stage claimed above 0 whose step runs on a toolchain host outside the oracle tier, and says so
;;   :verified  a stub run: the stage run on a tiny sample with the toolchain's commands first on PATH as stubs exiting 99
;;              (doc/CROPS-SCORE.md, "The stub runs")
;; Not a host toolchain: Arbace's own executables, TamaGo's go (the seed's toolchain, pinned by seed/goroot.sha256, its
;; sources Go forms in tamago/cmd/), the frozen jar of arbace-for-java-26-v4 (pinned by test/oracle/frozen-jar.sha256).
;; The JDK beyond that jar (jdk26u's build) counts. Sources: doc/ORACLE-RECORDS-SURVEY.md on mac/oracle-records-cpp2 (§1.2's
;; inventory, the crops' "As built"), the scripts at each ref (the evidence lines), 2026-11-06.
